@startuml View the System Status

actor User
actor Backend
participant Frontend

note left of User
  Backend is in operation, or it gives an error response.
  User has a web browser and the address of the page.
end note

User -> Frontend: User opens the page of the application in the browser.
Frontend -> User: Frontend shows User the waiting message for the status.
Frontend -> Backend: Frontend sends the request GET /status to Backend.
Backend -> Frontend: Backend sends the response with the state and the time of the check to Frontend.
alt Backend sends an error response
Backend -> Frontend: Backend sends the error response with the error code and the trace identifier to Frontend.
Frontend -> User: Frontend shows User the heading that the information is not available, the text for the error code, and the trace identifier.
note right
  The text is in the language of the page. Frontend does not show the members title and detail of the error response.
end note
end
alt Backend gives no response
Frontend -> User: Frontend shows User the heading that the information is not available and the text that the service gives no response.
note right
  There is no trace identifier in this case.
end note
end
alt Backend sends a response that Frontend cannot read
Frontend -> User: Frontend shows User the heading that the information is not available and the text that the response of the service is not valid.
note right
  There is no trace identifier in this case.
end note
end
Frontend -> User: Frontend shows User the text for the state and the time of the check, in the language of the page.
note right
  Step 4: Frontend shows the state as
  English: The system is up.
  English: The system is degraded.
  German: Das System läuft.
  German: Das System ist eingeschränkt.
end note
User -> User: User reads the state of the system.

note left of User
  The page shows the state of the system (up or degraded).
  The page shows the time of the check.
end note
note left of User
  The page shows the heading that the information is not available, and the text for the cause.
  The page shows no state and no time of the check.
end note
@enduml
